v1.0.54 build 58: Picker body stateful + faster expand animation

- _PickerBody converted from StatelessWidget to StatefulWidget, with
  FixedExtentScrollController held in State. Before, every build() of the
  picker body (e.g. during AnimatedSize animation frames) created a new
  controller — CupertinoPicker would briefly reset to initialItem on each
  repaint, contributing to the visual stutter during expand.
- AnimatedSize 300ms → 220ms, easeInOutCubic → easeOutCubic (faster
  perceived expansion, ~27% shorter animation window).
- Closed-state SizedBox.shrink() → SizedBox(width: double.infinity) so the
  collapsed branch has explicit width and the animation interpolates from
  a known base width instead of zero.
- Build 57's `RepaintBoundary` around the modal ListView and BoxShadow
  removal reverted (no measurable benefit on emulator, kept for
  cleanliness).
